    summary: "Loop 001 daily digest for 2026-11-01, generated from research-watcher output/latest/hits.jsonl (116 hits across 27 queries, scan regenerated 2026-11-01 06:03 KST via 'bash run.sh scan', 0 source errors, collected_at 2026-10-31T21:02 UTC). Unlike the previous six cycles, the score-9 top band was NOT recycled: the 3 live GSE328275 / GSE328422 / GSE326553 / GSE281463-64-65 accessions were all already on the page, but four genuinely new score-9 accessions entered the scan today (GSE311507, GSE346380, GSE348495, and the GSE281462/64/65 chromatin-interaction bundle with GSE281463 already retained), so the actionable harvest today comes from a genuinely fresh top band plus the score-6 ladder, after accession-level dedupe against the page-level GSE retention set (24 accessions retained on the page; 102 NOVEL accessions remain of today's 116, with the NOVEL score distribution 9:6 / 6:29 / 4:50 / 3:4 / 2:3 / 1:5 / 0:5; the three picks below are all accession-level NOVEL, verified against their NCBI GEO esummary and PubMed records for title, depositor abstract, taxon, sample count, pdat, gds_type, PMID and DOI rather than title-matching alone). Signal 1 is GSE311507 (Homo sapiens, n=16, pdat 2026/06/01, PMID 42185641, NPJ Precision Oncology, doi:10.1038/s41698-026-01509-8): a mechanistic platform that converts transcriptomic diversity into drug-actionable tumor states by integrating multi-cohort RNA-seq from 727 tumors across five independent datasets with genome-scale CRISPR dependency maps and pharmacologic screening, defining four distinct tumor survival circuits in HPV-negative HNSCC - a proliferative axis (MYC, MET/FAK, inflammatory and translational programs), an epithelial-differentiated/adhesion program, an EMT-like state with stromal activation, and mitochondrial/oxidative metabolic states - each mapping to a selective liability (mitotic/autophagy control, ERBB/PI3K and cadherin signalling, OXPHOS/mitochondrial translation, and G2/M-integrin-Notch respectively), culminating in a machine-learned 13-gene transcriptomic predictor of EGFR-inhibitor response (erlotinib-responsive tumours, R = 0.93) validated in prospectively collected fresh patient-derived 3D microtumors and outperforming EGFR expression itself. Signal 2 is GSE342551 (Canis lupus familiaris, n=39, pdat 2026/09/30, PMID 42774025, Frontiers in Immunology, doi:10.3389/fimmu.2026.1906638) with companion GSE342969 (n=5): a multiomic immune-and-metabolic aging reference built in a cohort of senior and young beagle dogs, combining untargeted serum metabolomics in 50 canines (25 senior / 25 young), bulk PBMC RNA-seq in 39 (19 senior / 20 young), and scRNA-seq in 30 (15 senior / 15 young) yielding approximately 318,000 PBMC transcriptomes - the largest canine single-cell dataset to date - resolving 27 distinct immune populations, with age-associated loss of naive lymphocytes, expansion of selected myeloid and Th1-like effector subsets, coordinated suppression of cell-cycle, DNA-repair and mitochondrial pathways in adaptive immune cells, enrichment of inflammatory signalling in innate immune cells, and depletion of ether-linked and other membrane-associated serum lipids. Signal 3 is GSE313628 (Homo sapiens, n=16, pdat 2026/09/14, PMID 42744797, Cell Death & Disease, doi:10.1038/s41419-026-09283-y): MIC13-mediated hepato-encephalopathy modelled with patient-derived iPSC carrying the pathogenic c.260-2A>G splice variant, differentiated into induced hepatocytes (iHeps) that reproduce the cristae defects seen in patient samples, with comprehensive multiomics showing disrupted amino-acid turnover, accumulation of TCA and urea-cycle intermediates, profound alteration of one-carbon metabolism affecting methylation potential, redox homeostasis and detoxification, impaired lipid metabolism with incomplete beta-oxidation, increased ketogenesis and diminished lipid storage, and - the lane-relevant endpoint - extensive extracellular-matrix remodelling with enhanced cell migration indicating an EARLY FIBROTIC PHENOTYPE. The day's runner-up worth flagging for the AI-DD lane is GSE347270 'Systematic mapping of enhancers, silencers, and topological elements with prime editing deletion screens [Swap-seq PPIF screen]' (Homo sapiens, score 6, n=924, pdat 2026/10/10): a pooled twin-prime-editing plus flow-sorting tiling deletion screen that dissects distal and intronic enhancers, characterizes CTCF insulators, discovers a novel HDAC-mediated silencer class, and nominates hundreds of genomewide silencers - the largest single BB-relevant regulatory-element dataset in the scan.",
